{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "01VV", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-quasi-projective}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6c58f05a14141711ae21ed1163c8a75a909dc1490b6692d4b86857bea063f116", "source_text": "Quasi-projective morphisms", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c7230483e460da1003febd4ff6e07495e6e2e507c483ceca171d00719d6f04d0", "unit_id": "tag:01VV:title"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01VV", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\cite{EGA}", "REF_0002": "\\cite{H}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a9961c501e79b5c6f80d6ffa2ae1ed168254ac95652a70dcd587223d33dbc513", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe discussion in the previous section suggests the following definitions.\nWe take our definition of quasi-projective from <REF_0001>. The version\nwith the letter ``H'' is the definition in <REF_0002>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d349b08cb7827c4347a51e42641810a78a1eea01abf4d6c7ac314838b2278f38", "unit_id": "tag:01VV:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "01VV", "placeholders": {"FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001": "}", "FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001": "\\footnote{", "LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{reference}\n\\cite[II, Definition 5.3.1]{EGA} and \\cite[page 103]{H}\n\\end{reference}", "MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$X \\to \\mathbf{P}^n_S$", "MATH_0008": "$S$", "MATH_0009": "$n$", "MATH_0010": "$f$", "MATH_0011": "$f$", "MATH_0012": "$f$", "MATH_0013": "$S = \\bigcup V_j$", "MATH_0014": "$f^{-1}(V_j) \\to V_j$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-projective}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-H-quasi-projective-open-H-projective}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0003": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0003": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-quasi-projective}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:bb3edfce4c8a9fe950b66c91760669905e5f1f5466e628be0ad636b5821daecc", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1ac9436c13e7bd520b0cc75de0eddad1001c286e4ec75d3091ff38264f4756d3", "source_text": "<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> We say <MATH_0002> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>quasi-projective<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if <MATH_0003> is of finite type\nand there exists an <MATH_0004>-relatively ample invertible <MATH_0005>-module.\n<STRUCT_0003> We say <MATH_0006> is <TEXTITOPEN_0002>H-quasi-projective<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if there exists\na quasi-compact immersion <MATH_0007> over <MATH_0008> for some\n<MATH_0009>.<FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001>This is not exactly the same as the definition in Hartshorne.\nNamely, the definition in Hartshorne (8th corrected printing, 1997) is that\n<MATH_0010> should be the composition of an open immersion followed by a H-projective\nmorphism (see Definition <REF_0001>), which does not imply\n<MATH_0011> is quasi-compact. See\nLemma <REF_0002> for\nthe implication in the other direction.<FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001>\n<STRUCT_0004> We say <MATH_0012> is <TEXTITOPEN_0003>locally quasi-projective<TEXTITCLOSE_0003> if there exists\nan open covering <MATH_0013> such that each <MATH_0014>\nis quasi-projective.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:61104d1b32c3cdd3fe815f614e385f41fe12e7f821ae2984abb014b87cd24bf0", "unit_id": "tag:01VW:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01VV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{more-morphisms-section-quasi-projective}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:86ec2eecd570d0c8a4f479624baf284069e51967c1f2fc353abd21054aea9915", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:17279ce374a9e3a0852485ab042156f6202ba2b87132ffa46d855dae426971ae", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nAs this definition suggests the property of being quasi-projective\nis not local on <MATH_0001>. At a later stage we will be able to say more\nabout the category of quasi-projective schemes, see\nMore on Morphisms, Section <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ccfebe8e5b860ffe900ba41e97069595bf84c2c44fbaaad66d1ce7c81463656f", "unit_id": "tag:01VV:prose-0002"}
